  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Health and WASH response for newly arrived Sudanese refugees and host communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed response is an integrated Health / WASH approach to improve the health status and hygiene practices of 64.800 people in and around the Arkoum, Allacha &amp; Farchana 2 sites. IRC focuses on Health while OTOBPFE focusses on WASH. In these sites, IRC already provides primary health care, sexual &amp; reproductive health care, and malnutrition treatment with complementary funding (PRM &amp; UNHCR)</narrative>
  </description>
